.TH SCALEINN 1 "November 2026" "scaleinn-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scaleinn \- command-line interface for the Scaleinn cloud platform
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scaleinn
[\fB\-\-debug\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.br
.B scaleinn \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scaleinn
is a lightweight client for the Scaleinn backend APIs. It authenticates a root
or IAM user, remembers the selected organisation and project, and manages cloud resources through
the backend. It never contacts infrastructure services directly.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B configure
Sign in, select the organisation and the active project, and store the user's policies. Options:
\fB\-\-protocol\fR, \fB\-\-api\-url\fR, \fB\-\-object\-storage\-url\fR,
\fB\-\-verify\-ssl\fR/\fB\-\-no\-verify\-ssl\fR,
\fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR, \fB\-\-project\-only\fR, \fB\-\-with\-token\fR.
.TP
.B object\-storage list\-buckets [\-\-search TEXT] [\-\-output json|table]
List the buckets of the selected project.
.TP
.B ct list [\-\-search TEXT] [\-\-page N] [\-\-size N] [\-\-sort\-by FIELD] [\-\-sort\-direction ASC|DESC] [\-\-output json|table]
List the CTs (Linux Containers) of the selected project.
.TP
.B version
Show the version.
.PP
Service commands (run \fBscaleinn\fR \fICOMMAND\fR \fB\-\-help\fR for details). Services marked
with * are skeletons without API commands yet.
.TP
.B ice *
ICE virtual machines.
.TP
.B network
Networking category: vpc *, shared\-vpc *, ipam *, router *, security\-group *, reserved\-ip *,
cloud\-dns *. Each is also a top\-level command.
.TP
.B block\-storage
Block storage category: network\-storage *, additional\-disks *, snapshot *, os\-disks *.
Each is also a top\-level command.
.TP
.B images
Images category: marketplace\-images *, project\-images *. Each is also a top\-level command.
.TP
.B managed\-services
Managed services category: database *, docker *, load\-balancer *, waf *, vps *, alert\-manager *.
Each is also a top\-level command.
.TP
.B management
Management category: users *, secret\-manager *, groups *, organizations *, policies *, projects *.
Each is also a top\-level command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print debug logs to standard error. Secrets are always redacted.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.scaleinn/config.json
API URL and other non-secret settings.
.TP
.I ~/.scaleinn/credentials.json
Access and refresh tokens, the selected organisation and project, and the user's policies (mode 600). A new login replaces all of it. Passwords are never stored.
.TP
.I ~/.scaleinn/logs/scaleinn.log
Log file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 general error; 2 invalid usage or input; 3 authentication failure;
4 access denied; 5 network error; 6 local configuration problem; 7 backend error.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation: README.md in the source distribution.
